WEBVTT

00:56.090 --> 00:58.968
FILING FOR LOVE

01:03.264 --> 01:06.058
2013 YEONHYANG TEMPLE CUISINE RETREAT
NOV. 15 TO 22, 2013

01:30.916 --> 01:33.711
MOTHER JOO KYUNG-HEE,
REMEMBERED BY JOO IN-A

01:38.465 --> 01:41.176
Mom's resting place
has such crisp air.

02:00.821 --> 02:04.491
Mister, untie me!
Let me go right now!

02:04.533 --> 02:05.826
What are you doing to me?

02:05.909 --> 02:07.870
Mister, let me go!

02:07.953 --> 02:09.079
I have to get out of here!

02:09.163 --> 02:11.040
- I have to leave!
- Mom!

02:11.165 --> 02:12.541
- I have to get out!
- Mom!

02:12.625 --> 02:15.085
Untie me right now!

02:15.336 --> 02:17.671
What are you doing? No! Don't!

02:17.713 --> 02:21.508
- Hold on to her tight.
- No! Let me go!

02:22.343 --> 02:23.802
- Grab her tightly!
- No!

02:28.891 --> 02:30.934
Jumping from there
will cause too much trouble.

02:33.937 --> 02:35.522
You'll land smack on a hiking trail.

02:36.565 --> 02:39.193
It must've been a long walk up here.

02:40.235 --> 02:42.905
Why don't you put that will
and energy toward trying to live?

02:44.281 --> 02:45.574
Enjoy the clean air and go home.

02:45.658 --> 02:47.326
The walk down is much nicer.

03:06.053 --> 03:08.472
I think you missed the last bus.

03:10.015 --> 03:12.142
Are there really no more buses today?

03:12.726 --> 03:13.811
Where are you headed?

03:14.687 --> 03:16.313
- I'll drop you off.
- I'm too afraid

03:16.397 --> 03:18.816
to accept a ride from someone
who just tried to end his life.

03:19.358 --> 03:20.442
No, thank you.

03:22.236 --> 03:23.529
You have a point.

03:26.407 --> 03:27.366
Excuse me.

03:28.617 --> 03:29.993
I hope to see you again alive.

03:47.386 --> 03:48.470
Hello.

03:48.554 --> 03:51.140
I'm Lee Tae-kwon, the new recruit.

03:51.265 --> 03:52.266
I hope we all get along.

03:54.518 --> 03:56.645
There's one last person to introduce.

03:56.729 --> 04:00.357
Joo In-a beat her competition
for first place

04:00.441 --> 04:02.234
among her batch of new recruits.

04:02.359 --> 04:03.610
She's a true elite.

04:03.819 --> 04:06.321
I'll show what a first-place recruit
can do. Thank you.

04:06.989 --> 04:08.115
I hope we work well together.

04:13.412 --> 04:14.538
Cheers.

04:15.497 --> 04:16.540
Good job.

04:25.966 --> 04:28.677
Why is this group so silent?

04:30.721 --> 04:34.266
Ms. Joo, pour Mr. Jeon a drink.

04:34.391 --> 04:35.392
Oh, sure.

05:01.460 --> 05:03.712
So I heard you're the son
of Haemu Group's president.

05:04.171 --> 05:05.923
A third-generation chaebol heir
I’d only heard about.

05:09.259 --> 05:12.179
Then you must know
I'm not valued much as a son.

05:15.641 --> 05:17.309
Was that why you were struggling

05:17.434 --> 05:18.852
when we crossed paths back then?

05:21.939 --> 05:23.315
I hope we work well together

05:23.565 --> 05:24.608
Manager Jeon Jae-yeol.

05:33.075 --> 05:34.493
I really hoped to see you again.

05:37.037 --> 05:38.163
I'm glad I chose to live.

05:49.883 --> 05:51.176
What do you mean?

05:51.802 --> 05:55.097
Mr. Jeon headed this project
from the initial planning stage.

05:55.180 --> 05:56.765
It just need to be signed
to be approved

05:56.849 --> 05:58.141
and you want me
to omit Mr. Jeon's name?

05:58.225 --> 06:01.311
Ms. Joo, you need to see
the big picture here.

06:01.812 --> 06:03.438
Don't you see his stepbrother

06:03.522 --> 06:05.816
has been taking all the credit
since he joined the company?

06:06.984 --> 06:09.152
So what? Are you saying that's okay?

06:10.779 --> 06:13.365
- If the president were to hear...
- Oh, come on.

06:13.574 --> 06:16.743
All this is possible
because the president is allowing it.

06:19.371 --> 06:20.539
You've heard, haven't you?

06:21.081 --> 06:22.332
About Mr. Jeon's birth mother.

06:22.666 --> 06:24.334
He won't ever make it.

06:24.418 --> 06:26.920
We must side
with his younger brother.

06:27.671 --> 06:30.215
Fly to Dubai and close the deal.
There's a flight in two hours.

06:30.340 --> 06:32.009
- You need to hurry.
- In-a.

06:33.260 --> 06:35.012
This will only get you in trouble.

06:36.096 --> 06:38.974
This isn't even my project.

06:39.474 --> 06:40.517
It's the company's.

06:42.811 --> 06:44.313
Still, it's too unfair and wrong.

06:44.396 --> 06:46.189
You did all the hard work.

06:47.858 --> 06:49.067
It's enough for me
that you know that.

06:57.284 --> 07:00.996
Everyone's too cruel.
They're so mean and nasty.

07:02.039 --> 07:03.123
In-a.

07:06.960 --> 07:07.961
I swear

07:09.713 --> 07:11.798
I'll protect you
for as long as I'm here.

07:12.633 --> 07:14.551
Whatever happens,
even if the sky falls...

07:17.554 --> 07:19.222
I'll be on your side, Jae-yeol.

07:25.604 --> 07:27.397
This is so darn infuriating.

07:41.244 --> 07:42.287
So you were a couple.

07:45.123 --> 07:46.667
We were once a couple.

07:50.379 --> 07:51.380
Why did you break up?

07:53.298 --> 07:54.341
Just because

07:55.092 --> 07:58.095
he found someone
within his league to marry

07:58.720 --> 08:00.097
and I wanted to live
a life of my own.

08:01.098 --> 08:02.432
It's one of those boring
and obvious reasons.

08:03.141 --> 08:04.226
It's all in the past.

08:05.811 --> 08:06.812
Are you sure of that?

08:08.730 --> 08:09.731
What does that mean?

08:18.198 --> 08:19.366
There was a tip-off

08:20.200 --> 08:22.869
claiming you were having
an inappropriate workplace affair.

08:23.745 --> 08:26.289
That's you and the VP, isn't it?

08:54.568 --> 08:55.569
You came back.

08:55.819 --> 08:58.613
It has been a long time,
Vice President Jeon.

09:03.660 --> 09:04.870
I missed you.

09:09.082 --> 09:10.959
I think it was the day
I returned to the head office.

09:12.586 --> 09:14.713
He was just pleased to see me again.
It didn't mean anything else.

09:18.050 --> 09:19.384
It didn't mean anything?

09:20.677 --> 09:22.054
The situation I just witnessed

09:23.680 --> 09:25.015
would signify otherwise.

09:27.100 --> 09:29.728
Is this the vice president's
one-sided feeling?

09:30.979 --> 09:31.980
Or is there

09:33.315 --> 09:35.025
something left between you two?

10:02.636 --> 10:04.805
I don't want you to come here
whenever you please.

10:07.933 --> 10:09.643
- In-a.
- Take your hands off me.

10:11.019 --> 10:12.062
Let go.

10:18.568 --> 10:20.195
The VP and I...

10:21.488 --> 10:23.198
He's an executive,
and I'm just his subordinate.

10:23.698 --> 10:25.117
That's all it is.

10:25.659 --> 10:27.285
I have no residual feelings
toward him.

10:34.751 --> 10:36.628
To be honest, I suspected you
after I got the tip-off.

10:37.504 --> 10:39.923
So I investigated about you
and tailed you.

10:40.590 --> 10:42.300
I even followed you home
for a stakeout.

10:45.929 --> 10:46.930
I knew it.

10:47.472 --> 10:48.723
There's a reason you're the ace.

10:48.932 --> 10:51.852
I never imagined
the guy would turn out to be the VP.

10:53.854 --> 10:54.855
So, what now?

10:56.690 --> 10:59.192
What's your conclusion
as the handler of PM cases?

11:09.411 --> 11:10.453
I don't know.

11:12.664 --> 11:13.915
I want to believe

11:15.458 --> 11:17.127
everything you say at face value

11:18.837 --> 11:20.213
that it's all in the past

11:20.630 --> 11:23.008
and however the VP feels about you

11:23.884 --> 11:25.427
you feel nothing for him now.

11:26.511 --> 11:27.512
But...

11:29.222 --> 11:31.600
I think it's my heart
that wants to believe that.

11:38.148 --> 11:39.482
Give me some time.

11:40.692 --> 11:42.277
I'll think about it
as cool-headed as possible.

12:29.741 --> 12:33.161
EPISODE 7:
TO HER LOVER

12:37.207 --> 12:39.376
- Five packs of soju cups.
- Five packs of soju cups.

12:39.501 --> 12:42.254
- And five packs of paper cups.
- Five of those.

12:42.379 --> 12:44.839
- Two packs of plastic spoons.
- Oh, and seltzer water.

12:44.923 --> 12:45.924
- Seltzer water?
- Yes.

12:46.007 --> 12:47.509
- We didn't order any.
- For highballs.

12:47.592 --> 12:49.886
Okay, add seltzer to the list.

12:50.220 --> 12:51.972
And then...

12:52.055 --> 12:54.599
Mr. Moo, can you stay still?

12:54.683 --> 12:56.226
I'm finding it hard to focus already.

12:56.309 --> 12:58.979
I guess I'm excited. We haven't
held any workshop in a while.

12:59.562 --> 13:01.147
I did some thinking, you see.

13:01.356 --> 13:04.651
No workshop is complete
without a barbecue.

13:04.734 --> 13:06.027
It wouldn't feel right.

13:06.319 --> 13:07.612
Don't you think, White Blood Cell?

13:07.696 --> 13:09.030
You're right. It wouldn't feel right.

13:09.114 --> 13:10.782
- Right?
- Hae-young.

13:10.907 --> 13:13.952
Eleven people will drive there,
and the rest will take the bus.

13:14.077 --> 13:15.203
Okay.

13:15.287 --> 13:16.496
Send a list of names

13:16.579 --> 13:18.498
- to the bus driver.
- Okay.

13:19.249 --> 13:22.502
When did you two
get close enough to speak casually?

13:22.585 --> 13:23.920
You caught on real slow.

13:24.421 --> 13:26.589
Mr. Cha, did you finish
your tasks for the day?

13:26.673 --> 13:27.882
Why are you over here?

13:27.966 --> 13:30.135
Did you text the whole office?

13:30.260 --> 13:32.804
I will right now.
Gosh, I'm sick of your nagging.

13:33.596 --> 13:37.017
Hae-young. We should order
pork belly and pork neck.

13:37.100 --> 13:38.310
Okay, fine.

13:38.435 --> 13:39.602
- Will you order some?
- Yes.

13:39.686 --> 13:42.314
- Yes, buy some pork. A big chunk.
- Just pork neck.

14:07.672 --> 14:09.924
Assistant Manager Noh Ki-jun, is it?

14:11.134 --> 14:12.177
Can he be trusted?

14:12.886 --> 14:14.137
He's an arrogant punk.

14:16.806 --> 14:19.059
He's definitely not
the submissive type.

14:21.144 --> 14:22.479
What did he mean?

14:22.896 --> 14:24.439
That something that can't work
still can work.

14:24.939 --> 14:26.358
What cannot work

14:27.275 --> 14:28.610
and what can work?

14:31.029 --> 14:32.989
You're Haemu Group's vice president.

14:33.531 --> 14:35.200
Why would you mind a lowly employee?

14:35.784 --> 14:37.285
You must have
other important matters.

15:01.017 --> 15:02.018
Ms. Joo.

15:02.602 --> 15:05.271
- Yes, Hae-young.
- Haemu issued new credit cards.

15:05.355 --> 15:06.856
Give me your old one. I'll cut it up.

15:07.273 --> 15:09.526
- It's in my bag. I'll get it.
- Okay, thank you.

15:25.458 --> 15:26.501
See?

15:27.836 --> 15:28.878
Something that can't work

15:30.422 --> 15:31.714
still can work.

15:53.486 --> 15:56.239
Does that issue have to wait
until the next meeting?

15:56.448 --> 15:58.074
It is a bit too early to bring up

15:58.199 --> 16:00.910
although what you want
is what matters most.

16:02.996 --> 16:05.915
You met with Director Han, right?

16:05.999 --> 16:07.083
Yes, I did.

16:18.595 --> 16:19.637
Noh Ki-jun.

16:20.346 --> 16:21.723
Will you knock first?

16:23.141 --> 16:24.601
I'm cooking ramyeon.
Do you want some?

16:24.934 --> 16:26.060
No.

16:26.436 --> 16:28.938
- Don't you dare ask for a bite.
- Hey, A-jeong.

16:31.316 --> 16:33.985
What's your VP like?

16:36.696 --> 16:39.991
Why do you say "your VP"?
He's yours, too.

16:42.285 --> 16:43.286
You're right.

16:44.245 --> 16:45.413
He's my boss, too.

16:45.622 --> 16:47.248
Why are you
suddenly asking about him?

16:47.707 --> 16:50.960
I thought you were
trying to figure out Joo In-a.

16:52.170 --> 16:55.340
You rushed out saying
you wanted to figure out

16:55.423 --> 16:56.633
your relationship with her.

16:58.134 --> 16:59.177
Did you figure it out?

16:59.302 --> 17:01.137
I figured out one thing for sure.

17:02.555 --> 17:03.890
That she's a darn tough woman.

17:05.016 --> 17:07.352
- What does that mean?
- I don't know. Forget it.

17:07.810 --> 17:09.062
Enjoy your ramyeon.

17:12.106 --> 17:13.149
What the heck?

17:35.004 --> 17:36.256
HAEMU GROUP

17:36.339 --> 17:39.384
2025 HAEMU GROUP
STRATEGIC PLANNING JOINT WORKSHOP

17:39.467 --> 17:41.803
HAEMU TRAINING CENTER

17:48.268 --> 17:50.144
- Oh, dear.
- My goodness.

17:53.856 --> 17:56.025
Gosh. Are we doing a barbecue?

17:56.150 --> 17:59.404
Of course, Ms. Joo.
A barbecue is a must at a workshop.

17:59.487 --> 18:01.698
I like the way you think, Mr. Moo.

18:02.657 --> 18:04.075
- I'll help with the stuff.
- What?

18:04.617 --> 18:05.868
- No!
- Don't!

18:05.952 --> 18:08.496
Let me pretend to be
an easygoing boss.

18:08.580 --> 18:09.706
- But...
- Oh, gosh...

18:10.123 --> 18:13.251
That must weigh at least 20kg.
She's pretty strong.

18:13.376 --> 18:15.587
- Move the boxes now.
- Yes, sir.

18:24.887 --> 18:26.764
You have a clinical condition
of acting tough.

18:29.434 --> 18:31.185
STRATEGIC PLANNING JOINT WORKSHOP

18:35.732 --> 18:37.942
A TIME TO CONNECT TO GROW

18:38.026 --> 18:39.068
The Planning Team.

18:39.819 --> 18:40.862
Human Resources.

18:41.779 --> 18:43.072
And the Audit Team.

18:45.033 --> 18:47.619
I just said your team names,
and I'm shuddering in fear.

18:50.622 --> 18:53.583
You work so hard
to keep our company going.

18:54.125 --> 18:55.627
At this workshop

18:56.169 --> 18:58.296
I hope you can forget
your strenuous workplace

18:58.421 --> 19:00.048
and relax and have a good time.

19:13.645 --> 19:15.938
Hang on. Why aren't you in bed?

19:16.189 --> 19:18.316
Isn't it almost midnight
where you are?

19:18.441 --> 19:20.818
I'm exhausted. Mom nags too much.

19:20.943 --> 19:23.196
Can't you just do as she says?

19:23.279 --> 19:25.657
She said she's been having headaches.

19:25.948 --> 19:26.991
Okay?

19:27.075 --> 19:29.118
Sleep well.
I'll talk to you tomorrow.

19:32.622 --> 19:35.958
Mr. Ahn, you should
take time off work soon

19:36.042 --> 19:37.877
to fly to the US to see your family.

19:38.169 --> 19:39.837
I didn't know you were watching.

19:40.463 --> 19:41.464
It's a pleasing sight.

19:42.090 --> 19:44.050
Are the others getting ready
for the next program?

19:44.133 --> 19:47.261
Oh, we'd initially planned
a team-building exercise

19:47.345 --> 19:48.680
but the two team heads said

19:48.805 --> 19:51.224
playing a sport is the best way
to boost teamwork.

19:53.476 --> 19:56.646
2025 HAEMU
STRATEGIC PLANNING JOINT WORKSHOP

20:00.149 --> 20:01.984
Warm up well and properly
so you don't get injured.

20:07.073 --> 20:09.701
Can't we watch an educational video
instead of playing futsal?

20:10.660 --> 20:12.328
Haven't you heard, Ms. Yoon?

20:13.121 --> 20:16.332
Ms. Joo said the MVP of today's match
can take the day off tomorrow.

20:22.463 --> 20:23.798
What are you doing?

20:26.134 --> 20:28.511
My gosh. What's gotten into you now?

20:30.138 --> 20:31.723
Why are you suddenly so eager now?

20:33.766 --> 20:35.601
- Faster!
- Goodness.

20:35.685 --> 20:37.019
I see you don't exercise much.

20:38.688 --> 20:39.772
Okay, everyone.

20:40.356 --> 20:41.941
Both men and women will play

20:42.024 --> 20:44.026
- so be sure no one gets hurt, okay?
- Yes, ma'am.

20:44.110 --> 20:46.571
Don't do anything
too aggressive like tackling.

20:46.696 --> 20:49.407
- Let's put safety first.
- Okay.

20:49.490 --> 20:51.451
We can't do that
if we're playing a competitive sport.

20:51.534 --> 20:52.910
It's all about winning.

20:52.994 --> 20:54.954
Take one of these beforehand.

20:55.204 --> 20:58.082
- Let's build some energy first.
- Thank you.

20:58.166 --> 20:59.417
- "Build energy"?
- Thank you.

20:59.500 --> 21:01.127
Energy is an asset, too, these days.

21:01.210 --> 21:04.464
We must save up when we can
to use when we must.

21:04.547 --> 21:07.133
- Thank you.
- At a moment like this.

21:10.261 --> 21:11.721
- Here.
- Thank you.

21:14.640 --> 21:15.892
Thank you.

21:23.065 --> 21:25.109
Wait, what's going on?

21:25.401 --> 21:26.903
Are you not going to share?

21:27.487 --> 21:30.531
Isn't this against the rules?
Isn't this a foul?

21:31.574 --> 21:32.742
Hello, sir!

21:32.992 --> 21:34.118
- Hello.
- Hello, sir.

21:34.243 --> 21:35.828
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

21:36.287 --> 21:37.622
Mr. Jeon, sir.

21:37.955 --> 21:40.124
I thought you'd left
after the opening speech.

21:40.917 --> 21:43.669
I heard you'd planned something fun,
so I decided to come cheer you on.

21:43.753 --> 21:46.380
Will you be rooting
for the Audit Team?

21:46.464 --> 21:47.673
Of course not.

21:48.174 --> 21:49.759
You'll be cheering for HR, right?

21:49.842 --> 21:52.678
Let's see. I'm thinking of supporting
whichever is the winning team.

21:55.807 --> 21:56.933
That'll be our Audit Team.

21:58.226 --> 21:59.936
- That's no fun.
- What?

22:03.147 --> 22:05.316
Ignoring the process
and siding with the winner.

22:05.817 --> 22:06.818
Isn't that uncool?

22:11.823 --> 22:14.367
You speak as if you're the winner.

22:15.368 --> 22:16.410
Yes.

22:17.954 --> 22:19.247
Because I will win.

22:23.960 --> 22:27.588
Mr. Noh is excessively competitive.

22:28.840 --> 22:30.883
I don't think we can be teammates.

22:31.759 --> 22:33.094
How about we compete for real?

22:34.136 --> 22:36.389
Sir, are you really joining
the match?

22:36.806 --> 22:38.516
You have a meeting at 3 p.m.

22:38.891 --> 22:39.976
Cancel it.

23:06.127 --> 23:07.378
Kick it! Score a goal!

23:10.256 --> 23:11.257
What the...

23:12.508 --> 23:14.218
- Shoot.
- Stop! Stop it!

23:15.261 --> 23:16.554
- Ki-jun!
- Watch out!

23:17.263 --> 23:18.347
Kick it.

23:29.025 --> 23:30.902
Mr. Jeon! No!

23:31.027 --> 23:32.737
Mr. Jeon, are you all right?

23:32.820 --> 23:35.114
Are you okay, sir?
I told you to play nice!

23:35.197 --> 23:36.574
What should we do about you?

23:36.657 --> 23:39.410
What got into Mr. Noh?
Doesn't he know he should give in?

23:39.702 --> 23:42.246
Maybe he wants to be the MVP
to take tomorrow off.

23:42.330 --> 23:44.332
At this rate,
he might lose his job for good.

23:44.874 --> 23:46.250
It must be your leather shoes.

23:46.334 --> 23:47.585
- Wear my trainers.
- No, it's fine.

23:47.710 --> 23:50.630
No, please, sir. Wear mine.
That would be best for us all.

23:51.005 --> 23:53.507
- I'm fine.
- Mr. Noh is going too far.

24:15.404 --> 24:17.198
What the... Did you see that?
That was a foul!

24:17.281 --> 24:18.741
- Referee! Come on!
- Not a foul!

24:18.824 --> 24:20.576
- Get back up.
- It's not a foul.

24:20.660 --> 24:22.453
He didn't do anything wrong.
That was just a bump.

24:22.578 --> 24:23.579
Keep playing.

24:23.663 --> 24:24.789
That was uncalled for. It was...

24:24.914 --> 24:26.040
Sir, you can go ahead and score.

24:26.123 --> 24:28.751
- No, wait. Time out!
- What?

24:28.876 --> 24:31.003
Sir, go ahead. Score a goal.

24:31.087 --> 24:33.297
- What are you doing?
- Time out!

24:33.839 --> 24:35.424
You caught it all, didn't you?

24:35.508 --> 24:36.717
You filmed it, didn't you?

24:37.593 --> 24:39.428
Referee, VAR.
Let's watch the instant replay.

24:39.512 --> 24:41.639
- Boo.
- No, forget it.

24:41.722 --> 24:44.850
- Let's review the footage.
- You're being a nuisance!

24:44.934 --> 24:47.144
You're a nuisance.
That's uncool. Stop it.

25:05.162 --> 25:07.248
Let's keep things going!

25:07.331 --> 25:09.125
- Let's play!
- What the heck?

25:09.208 --> 25:10.835
Wait! That's not fair!

25:10.960 --> 25:12.420
Come on. Get the ball.

25:12.503 --> 25:13.671
- Bring it this way!
- No!

25:42.491 --> 25:43.576
Are you all right?

25:52.001 --> 25:53.669
You said you'd win at all costs.

25:55.129 --> 25:56.213
You must feel let down.

25:58.049 --> 25:59.925
Not exactly. It wasn't a fair match.

26:03.596 --> 26:06.348
Ms. Joo tripped you up on purpose.

26:06.849 --> 26:08.184
Let me apologize instead.

26:09.435 --> 26:11.187
In-a can be like that.

26:13.856 --> 26:15.232
What do you mean by "like that"?

26:16.567 --> 26:18.819
Oh, do you mean she has long legs?

26:20.988 --> 26:22.698
Do you have anyone like that?

26:23.783 --> 26:26.327
Someone who always takes your side
no matter what happens.

26:28.704 --> 26:30.706
Actually, we go way back.

26:36.670 --> 26:37.671
Sir.

26:38.964 --> 26:40.257
Are you hiding something?

26:42.051 --> 26:43.803
You speak too much as if to deflect.

26:44.720 --> 26:46.847
It looks like you're trying
to hide something from me.

27:05.366 --> 27:07.743
Mr. Choi got you a change of clothes.

27:08.410 --> 27:09.954
Shall I cancel
your evening plans, too?

27:12.915 --> 27:14.083
I live

27:15.126 --> 27:16.377
with a guy right now.

27:20.589 --> 27:21.590
Ms. Park.

27:23.425 --> 27:26.595
The nice guy you said you lived with.

27:28.305 --> 27:29.890
Is it Mr. Noh Ki-jun?

27:47.825 --> 27:48.826
What's with this?

27:50.578 --> 27:51.704
What the...

27:52.371 --> 27:54.123
Are you trying to smash the thing?

27:56.041 --> 27:57.168
Come and sit down.

28:03.048 --> 28:04.091
Take a seat.

28:10.848 --> 28:12.308
- Is it this foot?
- What the heck?

28:15.269 --> 28:16.437
It's this foot.

28:18.272 --> 28:19.815
- Let me see.
- No...

28:22.985 --> 28:25.196
It's not that swollen.

28:25.279 --> 28:26.488
Don't be silly.

28:26.947 --> 28:29.450
Look at this side.
My ankle is usually slim like this.

28:29.950 --> 28:31.327
What a crybaby.

28:33.704 --> 28:35.664
You hurt me
and now you're treating me?

28:36.957 --> 28:38.500
You tripped me up on purpose,
didn't you?

28:38.959 --> 28:40.878
How could you sabotage a teammate?

28:40.961 --> 28:44.215
Would the VP look bad
if he didn't get to score today?

28:44.506 --> 28:46.133
Why do you care so much about him?

28:46.550 --> 28:49.678
Your career at Haemu would've ended
if you'd gone any further.

28:50.429 --> 28:51.555
You should know
where to draw the line

28:51.639 --> 28:54.391
in front of your coworkers,
especially HR.

28:55.267 --> 28:56.852
Don't you know
they'd have avenged the VP

28:56.936 --> 28:58.562
even if the VP himself
didn't complain?

28:58.896 --> 29:00.022
Goodness.

29:00.856 --> 29:02.942
You've worked long enough
to know how things work.

29:03.859 --> 29:05.277
Why were you so childish out there?

29:10.741 --> 29:12.034
So that means you took my side

29:12.576 --> 29:13.661
and not the VP's.

29:15.246 --> 29:16.413
I'm not on anyone's side.

29:16.747 --> 29:20.209
I just did what a superior would do
to protect her subordinate.

29:30.552 --> 29:32.721
- Okay.
- What do you mean by "okay"?

29:32.805 --> 29:34.056
Your PM case.

29:34.890 --> 29:36.350
I think I can conclude it now.

29:37.059 --> 29:39.645
- Just like that?
- Other similar cases were closed

29:39.770 --> 29:41.897
without disciplinary action
when the subject denied the charges

29:42.398 --> 29:44.149
and no other definite proof
could be found.

29:45.734 --> 29:47.569
I couldn't decide

29:47.695 --> 29:50.948
whether I should investigate further
and drag the VP

29:51.365 --> 29:52.866
to the interview room to grill him.

29:55.411 --> 29:57.204
I realized something today.

29:59.415 --> 30:00.916
The way you both feel for each other

30:01.667 --> 30:02.793
is different.

30:08.507 --> 30:09.550
I believe you.

30:11.218 --> 30:12.303
I want to believe

30:14.888 --> 30:15.973
how you feel.

30:20.811 --> 30:21.895
How do you think

30:23.731 --> 30:24.773
I feel?

30:29.987 --> 30:30.988
What you did today...

30:31.947 --> 30:32.948
Was that really

30:33.782 --> 30:36.785
only just to protect
your subordinate?

30:44.543 --> 30:46.003
I showed you.

30:47.338 --> 30:48.464
Some things can work.

30:50.716 --> 30:52.301
I don't care how long it takes.

30:53.510 --> 30:55.471
Take a good look at your feelings.

30:58.265 --> 30:59.350
I'll wait.

31:19.119 --> 31:20.954
So Ms. Song, you were in the shower

31:21.288 --> 31:24.541
and it seemed like someone
filmed the shower booth, right?

31:24.625 --> 31:27.086
Yes, someone was clearly filming
with their cell phone.

31:28.379 --> 31:29.630
What did the culprit look like?

31:30.339 --> 31:31.465
Did you get a glimpse?

31:32.466 --> 31:34.843
I just got a glimpse
of the person's back

31:38.013 --> 31:40.849
and he was wearing
the men's T-shirt for our department.

31:44.311 --> 31:46.188
- So disgusting.
- That's crazy.

31:47.981 --> 31:49.316
An inside job.

31:50.943 --> 31:52.861
This is the lodging,
so there are no CCTVs around.

31:53.487 --> 31:54.822
Do you remember anything else?

31:55.697 --> 31:58.575
He must be using a white cell phone.

31:58.700 --> 32:01.578
What I saw was a white rectangle.

32:04.164 --> 32:05.207
Like a white cell phone?

32:05.290 --> 32:07.084
- I guess so.
- It's so gross.

32:07.209 --> 32:08.377
Everyone has that, right?

32:09.378 --> 32:10.462
This looks like

32:11.296 --> 32:13.006
a simple job to handle

32:14.842 --> 32:17.553
as long as
the male employees cooperate.

32:17.636 --> 32:19.138
And do what? Check their phones?

32:19.221 --> 32:22.891
Let's check only the white phones

32:23.058 --> 32:25.144
and he might have hidden
the phone he used to film with

32:25.727 --> 32:28.063
so we should check each room
for people's luggage.

32:31.400 --> 32:34.778
- You don't need to go that far...
- We need to check for sure.

32:37.072 --> 32:39.324
It may be an inconvenience,
but please cooperate.

32:39.408 --> 32:41.034
- Goodness.
- Goodness, no. We should do it.

32:41.660 --> 32:44.830
We cannot rule out the possibility
that the culprit is the Audit Team.

32:44.913 --> 32:47.583
To make it fair, let's have
one from Audit and one from HR

32:47.666 --> 32:49.835
conduct only the necessary amount
of verification.

32:49.918 --> 32:50.919
All right.

32:51.879 --> 32:54.298
Mr. Ahn, can you represent the HR?

32:54.590 --> 32:56.842
You're known to be upright and proper

32:56.925 --> 32:59.595
- so no one will complain.
- Yes, I understand.

33:17.779 --> 33:20.282
- Ms. Kim?
- Mr. Ahn, actually...

33:22.284 --> 33:23.327
You two look great together.

33:24.620 --> 33:26.747
- I didn't see anything.
- Yes, okay.

33:41.261 --> 33:42.804
Come on, Mr. Cha.

33:43.472 --> 33:45.974
You can't do this
as a member of the Audit Team.

33:55.150 --> 33:56.276
These were...

33:58.153 --> 33:59.696
These were from the barbecue.

34:04.326 --> 34:07.037
Never mind, Hyun-kyu.
Let's give the used ones to him.

34:07.454 --> 34:08.580
You can have these at home.

34:10.707 --> 34:11.792
Thanks.

34:22.678 --> 34:25.847
We searched through
the women's rooms just in case

34:25.931 --> 34:27.015
but couldn't find anything.

34:27.641 --> 34:29.476
We need to do everything we can.

34:32.521 --> 34:35.232
Are there no CCTVs near the entrance?

34:35.315 --> 34:38.735
Once the day breaks, I'll ask
the management and check right away.

34:39.069 --> 34:41.989
Anyway, you all worked hard
until this late.

34:42.072 --> 34:43.323
Let's go back and get some rest.

34:43.490 --> 34:45.367
All right. Great work.

34:50.038 --> 34:52.499
Mr. Ahn, you dropped this.

34:54.376 --> 34:55.836
- Oh.
- Huh?

34:56.086 --> 34:58.547
You smoke, Mr. Ahn? Since when?

35:00.424 --> 35:02.884
Once every now and then.
I smoke in secret.

35:03.594 --> 35:05.804
There's no need to smoke in secret
when you're at work.

35:06.430 --> 35:08.390
Do you want
to step out with me for a second?

35:08.682 --> 35:11.435
He must be using a white cell phone.

35:11.518 --> 35:13.520
No, I plan to quit very soon.

35:13.604 --> 35:14.896
Thanks, Mr. Noh. I'll have it.

35:15.606 --> 35:16.732
I don't want to give it back.

35:17.107 --> 35:18.483
- Why not?
- If you want to quit

35:18.567 --> 35:19.776
you should do it right away.

35:19.901 --> 35:21.069
Let me give you a hand.

35:21.153 --> 35:22.654
It's okay.
I'll quit starting tomorrow.

35:22.738 --> 35:25.616
No way. You need to make
these decisions right away.

35:25.741 --> 35:27.743
Mr. Noh, do not give it back.

35:28.076 --> 35:31.455
- No, ma'am.
- Gosh, you two are quite the tease.

35:31.538 --> 35:32.789
Give it back, Mr. Noh!

35:32.914 --> 35:36.126
Goodness, yes. Don't try to control
what someone else likes to do.

35:36.251 --> 35:38.045
And cigarettes
are quite expensive these days.

35:38.128 --> 35:39.129
Yes!

35:40.088 --> 35:41.381
This thing?

36:01.652 --> 36:03.362
What the...

36:04.696 --> 36:07.240
Why? What is it?

36:10.118 --> 36:12.287
Is this a camera?

36:15.582 --> 36:17.167
Mr. Ahn!

36:17.376 --> 36:18.794
I can't believe this!

36:22.506 --> 36:23.882
Have you lost your mind?

36:25.592 --> 36:27.052
Damn it.

36:34.267 --> 36:35.811
Look at all these.

36:37.479 --> 36:40.107
Looks like you didn’t care
the time or place when filming these.

36:40.357 --> 36:42.150
From the elevator ride to the office

36:42.275 --> 36:45.195
in-house cafeteria, restroom

36:45.278 --> 36:46.738
and the subway ride back home.

36:48.782 --> 36:49.783
Wait, how did you take this?

36:53.412 --> 36:54.496
No!

36:54.663 --> 36:57.249
Did you install cameras
under the staff members' desks?

36:58.333 --> 36:59.668
This is exactly that angle!

36:59.876 --> 37:01.962
Well, Ms. Joo, it's...

37:02.045 --> 37:03.213
How can you do this

37:03.338 --> 37:06.299
to your colleagues
whom you work with every single day?

37:06.550 --> 37:08.510
What do you take them for?

37:09.177 --> 37:10.971
All right. I get it.

37:12.389 --> 37:14.433
But I am fully cooperating, right?

37:14.808 --> 37:18.562
Blowing this up
won't do any good for the company.

37:18.645 --> 37:20.897
And it'll put our department
in a different position.

37:20.981 --> 37:23.191
- Think of our company's image, too.
- Sure, those are important.

37:23.650 --> 37:25.736
Our position and the company's image.

37:26.486 --> 37:27.571
That's why...

37:33.869 --> 37:35.579
we should blow this up
as much as we can.

37:35.996 --> 37:38.206
While other companies
are busy trying to cover up

37:38.415 --> 37:40.292
their in-house sexual assaults,
we'll be the company

37:40.375 --> 37:42.002
that punished
a spycam offender harshly

37:42.878 --> 37:44.296
to become a great example.

37:45.797 --> 37:46.798
Wait...

38:02.939 --> 38:03.982
Today

38:04.608 --> 38:06.860
I plan to eat at the cafeteria
for the first time in a while.

38:08.111 --> 38:10.197
Yes, sir. I'll call them right away.

38:10.614 --> 38:11.656
No.

38:12.699 --> 38:13.950
I'll go downstairs now.

38:19.206 --> 38:21.041
I don't like eating in the cafeteria.

38:21.124 --> 38:24.169
We have to eat so we can wrap up
Mr. Ahn's case and submit the report.

38:24.252 --> 38:25.420
Eat up.

38:25.545 --> 38:28.173
We have to eat something delicious
to work more efficiently

38:28.256 --> 38:29.633
and to put together a better report.

38:31.426 --> 38:32.677
But this is delicious.

38:33.261 --> 38:34.387
It's so good.

38:41.728 --> 38:42.771
What?

38:45.982 --> 38:47.108
May I join you?

38:48.693 --> 38:50.821
Sure, we didn't rent out the place.

38:51.112 --> 38:52.113
Have a seat.

39:06.127 --> 39:07.587
Jae-yeol is at the cafeteria?

39:07.796 --> 39:10.215
Yes, on top of that,
he sat with Ms. Joo

39:10.298 --> 39:12.717
and Mr. Noh Ki-jun
of Audit Team Three

39:12.801 --> 39:14.803
so it was a huge deal
in the Audit Team's office.

39:17.430 --> 39:19.808
My brother can be pretty sly, too.

39:20.725 --> 39:23.228
Well, I got to eat with Doo-gi,
the best

39:23.562 --> 39:24.729
of Audit Team One, didn't I?

39:26.523 --> 39:28.608
It's an honor, Mr. Jeon.

39:30.819 --> 39:32.112
How's work these days?

39:32.487 --> 39:34.698
Were you in charge
of our subsidiaries?

39:34.990 --> 39:37.325
Yes, I'm now in charge of the steels
and the pharmaceuticals.

39:40.579 --> 39:42.330
You're in charge
of the pharmaceuticals?

39:43.039 --> 39:44.916
If you're doing that now,
who used to be in charge?

39:47.252 --> 39:50.839
May I ask why you wish to know that?

39:51.423 --> 39:53.592
Well, it's not a big deal.

39:54.175 --> 39:56.344
Yesterday, I drank with people
from the pharmaceutical division.

39:56.636 --> 39:59.556
They said the Audit Team
used to pester them to death

39:59.681 --> 40:01.558
but not anymore these days.

40:02.517 --> 40:05.270
So I was wondering
if there was a power trip back then

40:05.353 --> 40:08.189
or if things
aren't working smoothly right now.

40:09.024 --> 40:10.358
But I guess
someone else was handling it.

40:11.109 --> 40:12.402
Yes, sir.

40:22.370 --> 40:23.914
I heard Mr. Noh played

40:24.915 --> 40:26.708
a big part
in the recent spycam incident.

40:27.125 --> 40:29.461
Yes, well, it's my job.

40:30.712 --> 40:33.381
He seems quite competent.
Why did you put him in charge of PM?

40:38.219 --> 40:39.346
I'm the type

40:39.804 --> 40:41.431
who's good at everything that I do.

40:46.978 --> 40:48.521
Gosh, so delicious.

41:20.804 --> 41:21.888
You two have

41:23.181 --> 41:24.766
a special relationship, don't you?

41:25.976 --> 41:28.353
Last time, I saw you two together
by chance

41:28.436 --> 41:30.939
while dropping Ms. Park off
at her place.

41:32.232 --> 41:34.484
Oh, is it discourteous of me

41:34.609 --> 41:37.070
to bring up something this personal
in front of your direct superior?

41:37.612 --> 41:39.197
Yes, it is discourteous.

41:42.283 --> 41:43.618
And what's so bad about that?

41:43.868 --> 41:45.453
The housing price in Seoul
has skyrocketed

41:45.537 --> 41:46.788
so it's nice and economical.

41:48.123 --> 41:49.124
You already knew?

41:50.375 --> 41:51.376
Of course.

41:52.669 --> 41:55.547
She's been to our place, too.

42:00.301 --> 42:01.302
Is that so?

42:05.056 --> 42:08.560
Since when did our company
begin to visit our employees at home?

42:18.486 --> 42:21.448
I'll have to ask to be excused.

42:21.990 --> 42:22.991
I was in the middle of work.

42:23.908 --> 42:24.951
Sit.

42:25.660 --> 42:27.495
We're sitting here at the same table

42:27.746 --> 42:29.664
so don't you think it's basic manners
to get up together?

42:33.001 --> 42:34.502
You have a point.

42:34.878 --> 42:36.046
I'll go with you, Mr. Noh.

42:36.463 --> 42:38.423
I almost forgot my manners
and sent you back alone.

42:39.174 --> 42:41.968
We were initially
in the middle of eating together.

42:42.510 --> 42:44.220
Please enjoy your lunch, you two.

42:44.345 --> 42:45.346
Let's go.

42:47.724 --> 42:48.808
Come on. Let's go.

43:02.489 --> 43:03.948
- Isn't it good?
- It is.

43:05.033 --> 43:09.037
We should never waste any food,
but I couldn't help it. What a shame.

43:10.205 --> 43:12.457
Anyway, this toast is really good.

43:12.540 --> 43:14.042
Is this your first time trying it?

43:14.125 --> 43:15.627
That place has been around forever.

43:16.211 --> 43:18.880
When I was new, the only fun I had
at work was getting this

43:19.005 --> 43:20.548
on my way to work
and eating it in the office.

43:21.549 --> 43:22.926
Did you get one
for the vice president?

43:23.843 --> 43:24.844
I don't know.

43:28.389 --> 43:30.141
He must be furious, right?

43:31.392 --> 43:33.311
How am I going to keep my career
in the future?

43:35.188 --> 43:37.398
Will you take responsibility
and protect your subordinate?

43:38.233 --> 43:39.692
So why did you act so cheekily?

43:40.902 --> 43:44.239
I mean, he was way too immature
for someone who's a vice president.

43:46.032 --> 43:49.661
Anyway, I can tell after today
that he's definitely still into you.

43:50.203 --> 43:52.413
Then what? Do you want to conduct
an additional investigation?

43:52.664 --> 43:54.999
No, you aren't into him,
so it doesn't matter.

43:56.501 --> 43:58.419
I guess some people remember

43:58.545 --> 44:01.089
their old relationship like the rose
from The Little Prince.

44:04.425 --> 44:06.845
- What do you mean by that?
- Don't you know it?

44:07.512 --> 44:09.013
The Little Prince comes to Earth

44:09.097 --> 44:11.349
and sees many roses
that are exactly the same-looking.

44:11.850 --> 44:13.017
Yet he returns to the planet

44:13.101 --> 44:14.936
where the rose
he spent time with lives.

44:16.688 --> 44:18.106
The Little Prince returns?

44:19.107 --> 44:20.483
Doesn't he live
with the fox on Earth?

44:20.567 --> 44:22.861
No, he returns to his planet.

44:23.444 --> 44:25.363
He wants to be responsible
for the rose he cultivated.

44:25.446 --> 44:26.614
No, he remains on Earth.

44:27.448 --> 44:30.285
No, he returns.
Do you want to make a bet?

44:31.452 --> 44:33.288
Bet? I'm in.

44:33.621 --> 44:35.874
We aren't betting on a wish,
but a penalty.

44:36.291 --> 44:37.292
Sure.

44:38.042 --> 44:40.336
"I'm returning to the star tonight."

44:40.461 --> 44:42.505
See? It means
he's returning to his planet.

44:44.424 --> 44:45.884
What? This is really sad.

44:46.926 --> 44:49.304
Why did I remember the story
as a happy ending? What is this?

44:49.721 --> 44:52.098
You must've interpreted this
as a happy ending back then.

44:53.558 --> 44:56.436
Why did he want to leave Earth
after the trouble of getting there?

45:00.315 --> 45:01.316
So I won, right?

45:02.650 --> 45:05.361
You must've been
an avid reader of children's tales.

45:07.238 --> 45:10.366
Admit to your defeat
and face your penalty.

45:11.868 --> 45:13.620
Admitted. What's the penalty?

45:16.789 --> 45:19.000
Now, what can I do here

45:19.542 --> 45:21.377
to turn this into a cruel fairy tale?

45:33.848 --> 45:34.974
What is it?

45:54.494 --> 45:57.038
Hey, Ms. Joo has finally gone cuckoo
in her head.

46:03.544 --> 46:04.963
Excuse me, Ms. Joo.

46:05.880 --> 46:08.258
Your hair...

46:11.886 --> 46:12.887
What about it?

46:15.056 --> 46:16.599
Isn't it adorable?

46:16.933 --> 46:19.018
I've been into these things lately.

46:26.067 --> 46:27.193
Get back to work.

46:43.042 --> 46:47.171
ART CLASS DIRECTOR

46:50.008 --> 46:51.217
Thank you.

46:51.426 --> 46:54.387
That's cute.
What in the world is that hairpin?

46:55.596 --> 46:58.016
Yes, right. I still had this on?

46:59.267 --> 47:00.393
How embarrassing.

47:00.852 --> 47:01.936
That's new.

47:02.395 --> 47:03.771
Is that the recent trend?

47:03.813 --> 47:06.774
No, it was a gift from someone

47:07.775 --> 47:09.277
as a penalty.

47:12.947 --> 47:13.948
Anyway.

47:15.116 --> 47:16.659
I don't have to come
as a model anymore?

47:17.452 --> 47:18.828
What's going on? Am I getting fired?

47:18.953 --> 47:21.122
I should've hired you officially
and paid you.

47:21.706 --> 47:25.293
The business has been slow,
so I've been shameless.

47:25.668 --> 47:28.254
Don't say that.
I did it because I wanted to.

47:29.380 --> 47:31.716
And you already know
that I needed this.

47:32.467 --> 47:33.593
Do you still need it?

47:36.971 --> 47:39.474
I've known you a long time, In-a.

47:40.391 --> 47:44.562
And lately, I've been thinking
that you might not need

47:44.645 --> 47:45.730
this time anymore.

47:46.939 --> 47:48.107
You've been laughing a lot.

47:50.068 --> 47:52.320
- Me?
- Yes, and you seem to be at peace.

47:54.030 --> 47:55.073
Tell me.

47:55.531 --> 47:56.824
You're seeing someone, right?

47:57.325 --> 47:58.826
Is it the one
who gave you that hairpin?

48:02.288 --> 48:04.624
No, this is way too...

48:05.291 --> 48:08.378
You're the flower of the Audit Team,
so why don't you put a flower on?

48:08.461 --> 48:09.837
All right.

48:11.839 --> 48:12.882
A pig.

48:13.424 --> 48:15.635
Next, a rabbit.

48:16.010 --> 48:17.136
Look to the side.

48:21.682 --> 48:25.061
- I can't.
- What do you mean? Why not?

48:26.479 --> 48:27.605
He's someone at work.

48:29.607 --> 48:32.777
In another country, there is
this phrase about dating at work.

48:33.903 --> 48:35.571
"Don't go number two where you eat."

48:37.698 --> 48:39.242
It means it's that insane.

48:39.325 --> 48:42.829
Why not? It's better than
holding it in and getting sick.

48:43.621 --> 48:46.290
I'm saying, who cares
if you do something crazy?

48:47.291 --> 48:51.170
Didn't you think this job was
also crazy before you did it?

48:51.504 --> 48:52.713
But after trying it

48:52.797 --> 48:54.924
it became the only escape
in your everyday life.

48:56.050 --> 48:57.718
Don't put a limit on yourself.

48:58.219 --> 49:01.931
Only when you break the limit
will you find new joy.

49:03.599 --> 49:06.477
Hey, Director.
You're good with words.

49:06.686 --> 49:07.937
You didn't know?

49:31.461 --> 49:35.047
RECREATIONAL ART CLASS
TONIGHT AT 9 P.M.

49:49.812 --> 49:51.564
Have I always been this pretty?

50:04.577 --> 50:05.620
You are pretty.

50:31.270 --> 50:33.981
AUDIT RESULT

50:39.237 --> 50:41.072
You didn't seem to eat much at lunch.

50:41.572 --> 50:42.698
You should have some.

50:44.492 --> 50:45.493
Okay.

50:45.993 --> 50:47.954
And you crossed the line earlier.

50:50.748 --> 50:52.375
You used me.

50:53.543 --> 50:54.669
I know that

50:55.670 --> 50:57.463
you like Ms. Joo In-a.

51:00.550 --> 51:02.510
I'm a very competent assistant

51:03.844 --> 51:05.680
and a woman who likes you.

51:08.349 --> 51:09.517
Ki-jun is

51:10.434 --> 51:11.936
a great guy.

51:13.563 --> 51:14.772
It was the first time I ran away

51:14.855 --> 51:16.524
feeling annoyed
that he found out about my situation

51:17.483 --> 51:20.027
and I didn't want to burden him.

51:20.653 --> 51:23.155
I didn't want to be
belittled before him.

51:31.664 --> 51:33.082
Why are you telling me this?

51:33.165 --> 51:35.835
I'm saying you have nothing on Ki-jun

51:37.878 --> 51:39.338
even for someone like you.

51:58.065 --> 52:01.152
HR REPORT
ON US EXPATRIATE

52:16.208 --> 52:17.918
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

52:18.878 --> 52:20.504
- Two toasts, please.
- Sure.

52:20.588 --> 52:22.131
- Please make them delicious.
- Of course.

52:24.008 --> 52:26.260
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

52:33.184 --> 52:34.602
What is this?

52:35.061 --> 52:36.437
What does he have to say now?

52:36.520 --> 52:38.439
HR HEAD AHN SEUNG-WOO, PERVERT

52:38.481 --> 52:40.149
MISSED CALLS FROM
HR HEAD AHN SEUNG-WOO, PERVERT

52:44.779 --> 52:48.157
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

52:48.282 --> 52:49.408
ASSISTANT MANAGER NOH KI-JUN

52:55.498 --> 52:57.291
Will you please pick up?

53:12.640 --> 53:13.641
Hey, Ki-jun!

53:13.849 --> 53:15.184
What's going on, man?

53:15.601 --> 53:17.311
You really got
on the vice president's good side.

53:17.812 --> 53:19.146
What are you talking about?

53:19.271 --> 53:20.981
Ms. Hong of HR told me everything.

53:21.065 --> 53:22.733
I heard you got assigned
as an expatriate to the US.

53:24.235 --> 53:25.236
What?

53:26.612 --> 53:27.697
I'm so jealous.

53:31.075 --> 53:33.703
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

53:38.040 --> 53:40.209
Goodness, Mr. Lee. Mr. Lee.

53:40.543 --> 53:42.002
Thank you for coming out
on your busy day.

53:42.712 --> 53:43.713
Yes.

53:50.052 --> 53:51.846
I can't have you keep calling me.

53:52.096 --> 53:54.014
Think of how desperate I am.

53:54.557 --> 53:56.600
I'm about to get divorced.

53:56.684 --> 53:58.060
My wife is now...

54:00.730 --> 54:03.274
She's banning me
from seeing my child, Do-yun.

54:05.443 --> 54:09.071
Can you help me
get a favorable arrangement

54:09.155 --> 54:11.365
or let me settle the case?

54:12.158 --> 54:14.034
Maybe the employees
can turn in petitions

54:14.076 --> 54:16.036
and say that I've worked hard

54:16.495 --> 54:18.706
and always had a great reputation.

54:19.874 --> 54:22.585
Well, even if I
personally made a move

54:23.377 --> 54:25.463
the Audit Team
is already set on this.

54:26.213 --> 54:30.843
I've also been
contacting Mr. Noh Ki-jun

54:31.552 --> 54:33.053
but he won't pick up his phone.

54:34.388 --> 54:37.183
Mr. Ahn, he's on a roll right now.

54:37.725 --> 54:40.060
He got a special promotion,
thanks to your incident

54:40.144 --> 54:41.729
and he even got a chance
to work in the US.

54:43.397 --> 54:44.440
You didn't know?

54:46.776 --> 54:50.070
Director Park, I hear your daughter
is getting married soon.

54:50.571 --> 54:51.655
Congratulations.

54:52.281 --> 54:54.200
Let me know when you have the date.

54:54.450 --> 54:55.910
I'd like to relay
my congratulatory message.

54:55.951 --> 54:58.579
Goodness, Director Park.
That wedding will be a big deal.

54:59.079 --> 55:03.375
Are you really willing to come
and share a message?

55:04.376 --> 55:06.587
Or do you think
a song will be better?

55:25.815 --> 55:28.275
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

55:28.484 --> 55:29.610
Why won't she pick up?

55:29.693 --> 55:30.778
JOO IN-A

55:34.907 --> 55:37.117
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

55:39.328 --> 55:41.705
Hey, have you seen Ms. Joo?

55:43.082 --> 55:44.250
Have you seen her?

55:44.708 --> 55:47.461
I didn't, but Seung-hee just told me

55:47.795 --> 55:50.714
that Ms. Joo suddenly showed up
and left with the vice president.

55:52.299 --> 55:53.342
Where did they go?

55:57.346 --> 55:58.472
What do you think you're doing?

55:58.556 --> 56:00.474
- What?
- About Mr. Noh Ki-jun!

56:00.599 --> 56:03.727
You did not say a word to him or me,
who has direct authority over him.

56:03.811 --> 56:05.229
How can you suddenly announce

56:05.312 --> 56:07.731
sending him away overnight
like he's some parcel?

56:07.940 --> 56:09.984
And you barged in there

56:10.401 --> 56:11.485
to nitpick over this?

56:12.444 --> 56:14.488
You dragged me out
of a meeting with the directors

56:14.572 --> 56:16.532
just to nitpick over
an assistant manager's position?

56:16.615 --> 56:18.200
It's not just his position.

56:18.284 --> 56:20.995
This is a matter of respect
for my duty and authority.

56:21.495 --> 56:23.539
You are not allowed
to appoint an employee like this

56:23.622 --> 56:25.165
if he has no reason
to be disciplined.

56:27.418 --> 56:28.878
This is unjust.

56:29.753 --> 56:30.963
And this calls for an audit.

56:31.922 --> 56:33.549
I've reviewed
the decision thoroughly.

56:33.924 --> 56:36.510
It's a loss to the business
for an employee with his performance

56:36.594 --> 56:38.929
and competence
to be cooped up doing PM duties.

56:41.682 --> 56:42.850
Is that really the reason

56:44.894 --> 56:46.687
and not because
of any personal feelings?

56:48.397 --> 56:49.690
It's the US expatriate position.

56:49.815 --> 56:52.443
That's a place
where every employee wants to go

56:52.526 --> 56:54.194
and it's a privilege
for an assistant manager.

56:54.737 --> 56:56.572
He'll also be promoted as a manager.

56:56.864 --> 56:58.532
Is this something
for you to be so angry over?

56:59.241 --> 57:02.077
In-a, don't you think
you're the one holding back

57:02.494 --> 57:04.955
a talented employee's career
because of your feelings?

57:06.540 --> 57:08.292
Can you honestly tell me

57:08.876 --> 57:11.211
that you are this furious
only due to official reasons?

57:16.717 --> 57:17.718
In-a.

57:18.719 --> 57:21.138
There are many decisions I can make.

57:22.222 --> 57:25.559
And among them, I believe I made
the most courteous one I could.

57:33.525 --> 57:36.236
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

57:37.237 --> 57:38.364
Mr. Noh Ki-jun.

57:42.409 --> 57:43.410
Mr. Ahn.

57:45.913 --> 57:48.582
I cannot have you visit
or contact me like this.

57:55.756 --> 57:57.007
Hey, you...

58:26.495 --> 58:28.497
EMERGENCY ROOM

59:13.167 --> 59:15.544
You can't drive like this.
Let me take you there.

59:33.854 --> 59:35.397
Is he still waiting
in the emergency room?

59:39.359 --> 59:41.862
No, it's okay. There's no need.
I'll call you back.

59:42.029 --> 59:43.447
I'll just get off here.

59:44.073 --> 59:45.365
It's still pretty far from here.

59:45.449 --> 59:48.327
Just past the intersection... In-a!

01:00:04.551 --> 01:00:05.761
It's heartbreaking.

01:00:10.641 --> 01:00:12.142
You must've been very lonely.

01:00:15.521 --> 01:00:17.106
You keep acting tough

01:00:19.900 --> 01:00:21.068
which is making it worse.

01:00:27.241 --> 01:00:28.408
Then will you

01:00:29.076 --> 01:00:30.494
answer my question...

01:00:38.377 --> 01:00:39.962
Why do you push me away?

01:00:53.934 --> 01:00:55.769
About your question, Mr. Noh...

01:00:57.396 --> 01:00:59.565
The real reason
why I keep pushing you away...

01:01:04.862 --> 01:01:05.946
I...

01:01:09.658 --> 01:01:10.784
I...

01:01:14.997 --> 01:01:17.916
FILING FOR LOVE

01:01:46.695 --> 01:01:49.114
Mr. Noh. I was scared. It was scary.

01:01:49.198 --> 01:01:52.534
I think you should come along
to the Jeju business trip, Ms. Joo.

01:01:52.743 --> 01:01:53.827
What are you doing?

01:01:53.952 --> 01:01:56.288
Are you sending an assistant manager
overseas because of your feelings?

01:01:56.496 --> 01:01:58.665
In-a, please just stay by my side.

01:01:59.082 --> 01:02:01.460
What's the real reason you sent me
to Audit Team Three?

01:02:02.085 --> 01:02:03.503
Was it to protect Jeon Jae-yeol?

01:02:03.754 --> 01:02:06.089
How do you expect me
to understand this whole situation?

01:02:06.173 --> 01:02:08.091
We need to talk right now!

01:02:08.550 --> 01:02:09.843
Oddly enough

01:02:09.927 --> 01:02:13.013
I have a habit of hiding the truth
when it matters most.

01:02:26.568 --> 01:02:28.570
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
